# double_free_scan's per-slot state bytes (heap/slotstate.rs): a byte
# array outside every verified invariant. Verus checks the indexing and
# the arithmetic (the addresses wrap); the verified wrappers (free, claim,
# pop, release, the batch loops, check_not_cached) only turn what `step`
# returns into aborts (`abort_pending`); none changes what the verified
# paths do. `commit`'s range lying in `init`'s reservation is not
# verified either (`mprotect` is specified only for its call).

# The arrays' initialiser: an array repeat of an element that is not
# `Copy`, which Verus does not take. It claims nothing, and it is
# evaluated at compile time; the harness checks that every entry is zero.
NO_ARRAYS	core library	Kani	discharged (Kani: heap::slotstate::kani_arrays::no_arrays_are_zero)	contract 2521126641, body none

# The byte at an address `byte` computes: a slot index below the
# watermark that `commit` precedes, in an array `init` reserved. That
# protocol is not a verified fact; it claims only the byte's identity
# (`slot_byte_id(at)`, under which SLOTS holds its permission), nothing
# about its value. The harness runs the body on a byte of its own array.
byte_at	raw pointer (internal)	Kani	trusted (partly checked, Kani: heap::slotstate::kani_byte_at::byte_at_is_the_byte; not checked: the `# Safety` contract, that `at` is a byte of a slot-state array that `commit` made writable and that the arrays live for the process, which is the protocol of `init`, `commit` and the watermark: the harness passes a byte of its own array; and the ghost identity its `ensures` names, `slot_byte_id(at)`)	contract 5560191, body 4214957818

# The double-free window's first value (theorem_double_free_window): a
# permission to the slot-state byte at every address, each FREE (the
# arrays are fresh anonymous mappings, zero-filled, never unmapped, and
# written only by `step`). Taken once, by SLOTS' initialiser, at compile
# time; SLOTS' invariant then carries each byte's value from one step to
# the next. No verified invariant ties the bytes to the caches or the
# bitmap (#397); the operations are vspec::byte's wrappers; the free's
# race is tests/loom/src/slotstate.rs. Pinned by
# tests::slot_bytes_axiom_is_taken_only_by_slots.
axiom_slot_bytes	allocator invariant	none (assumption)
